<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Houthis claim strike on oil facilty near Riyadh, accuse Saudi forces of pounding Yemen's capital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9cd59b32e9134116044912c2177d6e5838a6bef1f45b771f934e3dd7c705a1e0</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T14:31:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-houthis-blame-saudi-air-strikes-loud-blasts-rock-yemen-capital-sanaa--81b4ce29f4be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-houthis-blame-saudi-air-strikes-loud-blasts-rock-yemen-capital-sanaa" /><summary type="html">Houthi rebels accused Saudi forces of launching 26 strikes on Sanaa on Saturday after loud explosions rocked the Yemeni capital. The Iran-backed group said it struck an oil facility south of Riyadh, where flames and a large plume of smoke were seen rising from a plant belonging to oil giant Aramco.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>UAE investigators say Omani Flydubai co-pilot was planning 'terrorist' attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:941a3551bbd31a009e79799dcdb2b48e94aaec46b8ffc8ddf0499bf3135a60f6</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T06:17:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-co-pilot-on-flydubai-flight-was-banned-from-flying-by-oman-for-holding-extremist-views--d42f7d08990d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-co-pilot-on-flydubai-flight-was-banned-from-flying-by-oman-for-holding-extremist-views" /><summary type="html">The Omani co-pilot accused of attacking the captain aboard a Flydubai flight to Israel on September 30 attempted to carry out a "terrorist" attack, the United Arab Emirates prosecutor general said ​Saturday. The alleged assailant, identified as Omani national Hamam al-Hammami, had been barred from flying in his country due to his radical ideological views, several media reported.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu warns of 'very heavy price' if any country found to be behind FlyDubai incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:152f5744f67a1997387e625188d8f5edb8150f81f114ea43941851801ede86a2</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T13:55:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-netanyahu-warns-of-very-heavy-price-if-any-country-found-to-be-behind-flydubai-incident--ca93f0f1308d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-netanyahu-warns-of-very-heavy-price-if-any-country-found-to-be-behind-flydubai-incident" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Friday warned that any country or organisation found to be responsible for the violent clash on board an Israel-bound FlyDubai flight would "pay a very heavy price". While Netanyahu has alleged the co-pilot who stabbed his captain mid-flight had undergone "Islamist radicalisation", the motive behind the incident remains unclear.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'America is leaving Iraq, but Iran isn't: Withdrawal a massive strategic and tactical mistake'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8bcd3cff8ff487170e98a92edf0bc91ea06e6f8bf4c44784679a3dd8f8748b2f</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T10:11:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-america-is-leaving-iraq-but-iran-isn-t-withdrawal-a-massive-strategic-and-tactical-mistake---0b781c6b753d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-america-is-leaving-iraq-but-iran-isn-t-withdrawal-a-massive-strategic-and-tactical-mistake-1" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Bamo Nouri, investigative journalist and also Honorary Research Fellow with the Department of International Politics at City Saint George's University of London. He sees the end of the American military presence in Iraq as a profound shift in the balance of power inside the country. For him, the central question is not whether Iraq has formally regained sovereignty, but whether it possesses the political cohesion, security capacity and economic independence necessary to exercise that sovereignty.</summary></entry><entry><title>Flydubai hero pilot tells Modi 'I could not let all those people die'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6c13690d6b454f525d3832c49eaaeb54c4f7f9a02909126daa6238097546ad9</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:04:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-flydubai-hero-pilot-tells-modi-i-could-not-let-all-those-people-die--42220aab298b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-flydubai-hero-pilot-tells-modi-i-could-not-let-all-those-people-die" /><summary type="html">Smit Machchhar, the Indian captain who was attacked by his co-pilot onboard the Flydubai flight 1073 in an apparent attempt to crash the plane, on Friday told Prime Minister Narendra Modi that although he was severely injured in the altercation, “I could not let all those people die”. Although collapsed, he made a last-ditch effort and managed to push the door to the cockpit open.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Egypt warned Israel of 'major' Hamas attack: 'No world where Netanyahu's not aware' (Vivian Salama)</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c403da6327c43739528fc0f2d3e48b999bb84c88147c5c510df6965cd7f8422a</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T06:08:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261002-egypt-warned-israel-of-major-hamas-attack-no-world-where-netanyahu-s-not-aware-vivian-salam--f8a90c764c92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261002-egypt-warned-israel-of-major-hamas-attack-no-world-where-netanyahu-s-not-aware-vivian-salama" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Vivian Salama from Washington. An attorney and staff writer at The Atlantic, Salama has reported from more than 85 countries. Her latest investigation takes us back to September 26, 2023. As Israel's national security establishment gathered to commemorate the 50th anniversary of the Yom Kippur War and one of the country's greatest intelligence failures, Abbas Kamel, then Egypt's intelligence chief, made an exceptionally rare and discreet visit to Israel with a stark warning about the dangerous situation unfolding in Gaza.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi-led coalition accuses Houthis of striking Medina power station</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df6a9bdd29c1345fd256ae51f90d2ce1e6ba89f9c891d4f637c32ecb2e74f819</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T02:39:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-saudi-led-coalition-houthis-striking-medina-power-station--f1bafc85decd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-saudi-led-coalition-houthis-striking-medina-power-station" /><summary type="html">Yemen’s Iran-backed Houthis struck an electricity distribution station supplying the Prophet’s Mosque in Saudi Arabia’s holy city of Medina, the Saudi-led coalition said Thursday, drawing condemnation across the Muslim world. The Houthis denied involvement in the drone attack, which came as fighting intensified between government forces and rebels in Yemen.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu says Flydubai co-pilot was radicalised as UAE probes terror link</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af7433891779335c4cdd2cfd36d455e2b28a705a2c0e06d66d9c4be120e48cde</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T23:27:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-netanyahu-flydubai-co-pilot-uae-terror-link--c49875f08b16.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-netanyahu-flydubai-co-pilot-uae-terror-link" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Thursday the co-pilot accused of attacking a Flydubai flight carrying mostly Israelis had undergone “Islamist radical indoctrination”, as UAE authorities investigated a possible terror link. The captain and passengers overpowered the suspect before the plane made an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia on Wednesday.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>AI deepfake of BBC report falsely links Indians to FlyDubai hijacking attempt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e0fa0bf142b587df9472c4e2305c901a0689c9315255ece1deada9ced62c50f</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T21:11:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/fake-bbc-report-falsely-implicates-indian-passenger-and-pilot-in-flydubai-hijacking-attempt--0c0d3e8a964c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/fake-bbc-report-falsely-implicates-indian-passenger-and-pilot-in-flydubai-hijacking-attempt" /><summary type="html">False videos are circulating after the attempted hijacking of a FlyDubai flight between Dubai and Tel Aviv. One fake "BBC" report falsely claims an Indian passenger was behind the incident and links him to the stabbed pilot, Smit Machchhar. The video though, is an AI-generated deepfake: the BBC never broadcast it, and its footage and audio were doctored. A second clip was also misrepresented and filmed in Dubai, not over where the incident occurred. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Sheer devastation: '80 percent of Gazan infrastructure has been destroyed'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2dec7f82dfd2f6255144f93c0e73df14438323e5d9bd203b5a901f29f4f5ddd</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:16:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sheer-devastation-80-percent-of-gazan-infrastructure-has-been-destroyed--aa956df4e191.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sheer-devastation-80-percent-of-gazan-infrastructure-has-been-destroyed" /><summary type="html">New images posted this week by Google Maps show the utter destruction in Gaza. It's been estimated that 61 tonnes of rubble need to be cleared – that's 20 times the amount of rubble generated in all wars across the world over the last 18 years.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's Netanyahu says co-pilot tried to crash Tel Aviv-bound plane</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eaf62ea54ac64743195599868b4ad4266eef8f168de7c306f06c32bd2c5a7a85</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T10:00:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261001-israel-s-netanyahu-says-co-pilot-tried-to-crash-tel-aviv-bound-plane--0359d75b68e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261001-israel-s-netanyahu-says-co-pilot-tried-to-crash-tel-aviv-bound-plane" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 1: A FlyDubai flight was diverted to Saudi Arabia after the pilot was stabbed by his co-pilot in what the Israeli media are calling a terror attack. The co-pilot was detained by off-duty pilots on board and passengers before making a safe landing in Saudi Arabia. Also in the news, Cornell University's college campus culture is back under scrutiny after a shocking sexual assault claim. Plus, a man learns that Singapore does not take AI slop lightly.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Indian pilot hailed as 'hero' after being allegedly stabbed by co-pilot on Israel-bound flight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45341de8e0f4aa3805c149446b445ebc4cd9c8db9548b10916c907d67e04eaa9</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T08:16:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-indian-pilot-hailed-as-hero-after-being-allegedly-stabbed-by-co-pilot-on-israel-bound-fligh--1da14e9867a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-indian-pilot-hailed-as-hero-after-being-allegedly-stabbed-by-co-pilot-on-israel-bound-flight" /><summary type="html">Smit Machchhar, the Indian pilot whose co-pilot allegedly stabbed him during the Israel-bound flight, was hailed as a "hero" by his friends and neighbours in Dubai Thursday. The Indian embassy in the United Arab Emirates said that he was "in good health".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Flydubai cockpit incident turns focus to crew-related hijackings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:415f4a47d7e9b13e614ea6017d1d666a700002a92a80d28d57fbcecbf1594d2a</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T08:01:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-flydubai-cockpit-incident-turns-focus-to-crew-related-hijackings--374ea865bcb1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-flydubai-cockpit-incident-turns-focus-to-crew-related-hijackings" /><summary type="html">The pilot of the Flydubai flight is suspected of having stabbed his copilot midflight in an apparent attempt to crash the plane. The incident has turned focus to similar incidents in the past, where deliberate crashes or near crashes have been instigated by on or off-duty crew.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Pilot wounded in Flydubai incident is ‘in good health’, Indian embassy in UAE reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1353032529ac7b7a6efc91e3972d31668a6d77cf09af29e75878bf742da2ed9</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T05:58:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-live-flydubai-suspends-flights-to-and-from-israel-after-pilot-attack--44a1c7b6f345.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-live-flydubai-suspends-flights-to-and-from-israel-after-pilot-attack" /><summary type="html">Smit Machchhar, the pilot wounded in a violent altercation in an Israeli-bound passenger jet Wednesday, is “in good health and recovering well”, India’s embassy in the United Arab Emirates said Thursday. Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu earlier alleged the co-pilot believed to have stabbed Machchhar had undergone “Islamist radical indoctrination”, without providing evidence for the claim. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Like a 'rollercoaster': passengers describe harrowing flydubai flight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e34a173269ef0f07d5b8807523615b7f253837c6a536e636a3b8831a375ef756</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T21:31:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/like-a-rollercoaster-passengers-describe-harrowing-flydubai-flight--9d7009b2f605.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/like-a-rollercoaster-passengers-describe-harrowing-flydubai-flight" /><summary type="html">As flight FZ 1073 from Dubai to Tel Aviv approached the Jordanian border on Wednesday, passengers knew in an instant that something was wrong when the plane began plummeting from the sky in a rapid dive. It was like "we were having very big turbulence, but there was no turbulence", passenger Almog Italie told AFP, describing the sensation of losing thousands of feet of altitude in seconds as similar to riding a "rollercoaster". FRANCE 24's August Hakansson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Attempted terror attack’: What happened on board the rerouted Flydubai flight?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df49f0fc63230cb228c7fcd6d0be0a8991107cc5218023ee122da67aa3469e5c</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T16:04:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-attempted-terror-attack-what-happened-on-board-the-rerouted-flydubai-flight--427fdbaf19b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-attempted-terror-attack-what-happened-on-board-the-rerouted-flydubai-flight" /><summary type="html">The co-pilot of a flight from Dubai to Tel Aviv ​tried ‌to crash the plane after stabbing the pilot, but passengers then ⁠held him down while other pilots landed the plane safely in Saudi Arabia, Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said ‌on Wednesday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mixed reactions in Iraq on final day of US-led coalition withdrawal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:976247efce50b857036fffb444c501a41942911013e25042feff0a4c9a43442d</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T11:27:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-mixed-reactions-in-iraq-on-final-day-of-us-led-coalition-withdrawal--29152cc8659b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-mixed-reactions-in-iraq-on-final-day-of-us-led-coalition-withdrawal" /><summary type="html">The US military announced on Wednesday that it has completed the withdrawal of all American troops from Iraq, ending a 12-year mission to fight the Islamic State group. The last US troops left an air base in northern Iraq under a deal between Baghdad and Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu says Israel is preparing for other ‘potential threats’ after pilot tried to crash plane</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f85a33e4a840a7a7add567810e6d33cb3037f90ee4b9d01c91fde8aa0667ccd</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T08:25:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260930-israel-bound-flight-diverted-to-saudi-arabia-after-brawl-between-pilots--5eb43950f821.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260930-israel-bound-flight-diverted-to-saudi-arabia-after-brawl-between-pilots" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said that one of the pilots of an Israel-bound flight had tried to kill the other and crash the plane, but that passengers and crew had managed to overpower him and safely land the plane in Saudi Arabia. All the passengers have since arrived in Israel, and Saudi authorities have arrested and are interrogating the alleged assailant.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US forces leave Iraq, raising fears of Iran-backed militias amid power vacuum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5fe316183436b57f6442f42c34ce999d08acd46734151a9d09cfa21466088af</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T01:04:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260930-us-forces-leave-iraq-raising-fears-of-iran-backed-militias-amid-power-vacuum--6f5d6f0a7ff6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260930-us-forces-leave-iraq-raising-fears-of-iran-backed-militias-amid-power-vacuum" /><summary type="html">US forces are withdrawing from their remaining bases in Iraq on Wednesday, completing a pullout agreed under former president Joe Biden as fears grow over the security vacuum it could leave. Iraqi officials and analysts warn the departure could embolden Iran-backed militias and give Islamic State group fighters room to rebuild their capabilities.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Settler raid on West Bank village injures Israeli forces, drawing rare government rebuke</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c88d3c27e79ee4047416487f33be44ef29c71ca9e61a84b7397a0322dc02b57</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:35:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-settler-raid-on-west-bank-village-injures-israeli-forces-drawing-rare-government-rebuke--5c1887db9a8c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-settler-raid-on-west-bank-village-injures-israeli-forces-drawing-rare-government-rebuke" /><summary type="html">More than 100 Israeli settlers stormed a village in the occupied West Bank early on Tuesday, setting fire to Palestinian properties and wounding three members of Israel's security forces. The raid, which drew rare government condemnation, came as the military attempted to accompany a Palestinian family back to their home after they had been displaced by earlier settler attacks.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Video shows Iranian police beating, sexually humiliating teenage detainee</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be47783fd9f5630914d762615fa0cb2a502030b05301185f9818dc10a3718d03</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T09:56:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-iran-police-video-teenage-detainee-abuse--3fd5b34486fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-iran-police-video-teenage-detainee-abuse" /><summary type="html">A video posted in mid-September showing Iranian police officers beating and sexually harassing an arrested teenage boy has caused widespread outrage in Iran. Experts say such mistreatment of people accused of common crimes is frequent in Iran, but the footage provides rare visual evidence of what they describe as a recurring practice within the police force.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran says it expects US response Tuesday on plan to reopen Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:151c6c8d59bcf8c45c4a2235746b5da475211fff44f82171f26dc44e52d0e793</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T06:32:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-iran-says-expects-us-response-tuesday-plan-reopen-strait-of-hormuz--63f87509ea04.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-iran-says-expects-us-response-tuesday-plan-reopen-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">Iran's Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi said Tehran expects Washington to respond to its proposal to reopen the Strait of Hormuz on Tuesday. In exchange for reopening the vital shipping route, Tehran is seeking guarantees including a regional ceasefire, the lifting of sanctions on its oil sector and an end to the US naval blockade.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Trump 'flips &amp; flops' with Iran between making a deal and threats to attack in ‘devastating fashion’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10e1113a23f72555a468a97bb54a09f3bca3309d48f5391f97d021f047468051</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T18:18:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260928-saudis-furious-trump-flips-flops-between-deal-with-iran-and-attacks-in-devastating-fashion--c70fe6067205.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260928-saudis-furious-trump-flips-flops-between-deal-with-iran-and-attacks-in-devastating-fashion" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Stimson Center. She describes the US-Iran conflict as a dangerous combination of military escalation, diplomatic ambiguity and political calculation. Slavin sees an absence of true diplomacy: the recent indirect contacts between Washington and Tehran, mediated by Qatar, have been too limited and too fragile to produce any serious breakthrough. For her, this amounts to "kabuki diplomacy": they half engage while positioning themselves against any appearance of compromise.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Trump expects Iran talks next week after rejecting seven-day truce proposal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81f98408228f2190af5c11c5d4ec6c72fc3c87b40e16aed6a99f2eb640b84e0d</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T22:10:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260927-trump-expects-iran-talks-next-week-after-rejecting-seven-day-truce-proposal--ec7a283e05ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260927-trump-expects-iran-talks-next-week-after-rejecting-seven-day-truce-proposal" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Sunday said he expected talks with Iran to resume next week, despite rejecting Tehran’s proposal for a seven-day truce followed by the reopening of the Strait of Hormuz. Trump raised the possibility of renewed air strikes on Iran but also said he anticipated further negotiations.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel revokes Dutch diplomats' West Bank credentials over settlement goods ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79bd1039cc04d89769f1e6fdd0d101e346ee5fa2a4a183d5d4c5d2ab61b85121</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T21:47:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260927-israel-revokes-dutch-diplomats-credentials-settlement-sanctions--c9e6069f5a47.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260927-israel-revokes-dutch-diplomats-credentials-settlement-sanctions" /><summary type="html">Israel will revoke the diplomatic accreditation of Dutch officials based in the occupied West Bank after the Netherlands began enforcing a ban on goods from Israeli settlements, Foreign Minister Gideon Saar said Sunday. The officials have seven days to surrender their Israeli-issued diplomatic papers, he added.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East: Palestinians plan first local elections in 20 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0229787872157a3748f25374d5a729d38da1197e3bff0fdaf25434f41bf731e1</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T12:29:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east-palestinians-plan-first-local-elections-in-20-years--211e8e3008fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-palestinians-plan-first-local-elections-in-20-years" /><summary type="html">Oliver McTernan, Director and co-founder of Foward Thinking in London, is our guest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Middle East: An art centre for children in occupied West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7202c85f1999ff36c11892e29d4b36e72f6464b00cd47a31ebde8595d88791a5</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T10:10:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east-an-art-centre-for-children-in-occupied-west-bank--a778dd857aa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-an-art-centre-for-children-in-occupied-west-bank" /><summary type="html">To help children process their experiences of war, an art center has been established in the West Bank.</summary></entry><entry><title>Middle East: Iran proposes Hormuz plan, Donald Trump reportedly refuses</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7e45f8146eccab2a9121682d08a527d776bf52d0cd7a531da357334f1c08f73</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T09:35:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east-iran-proposes-hormuz-plan-donald-trump-reportedly-refuses--0c236672cf1a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-iran-proposes-hormuz-plan-donald-trump-reportedly-refuses" /><summary type="html">The United States had yet to publicly respond on Saturday after Iran offered a plan to reopen the strategic Strait of Hormuz, though reports indicated that President Donald Trump had rejected the proposal. The waterway key to the world's oil supply is central to the conflict between the US and Iran, which is at a stalemate after nearly seven months, though new mediation efforts took place this week.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israelis, Palestinians must 'reboot relations': Absence of diplomatic route means 'perpetual war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94d3f513c1cdddd4aa89fb5b18000f85212ed32e2d4ac3cd2d5abe92c5616799</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T07:50:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israelis-palestinians-must-reboot-relations-absence-of-diplomatic-route-means-perpetual-war--a967accb3eb5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israelis-palestinians-must-reboot-relations-absence-of-diplomatic-route-means-perpetual-war" /><summary type="html">Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Yossi Mekelberg, Senior Consulting Fellow of the Middle East and North Africa Programme at Chatham House. Can Israel continue to define its future primarily through security and territorial control? Mekelberg challenges the notion that military operations, incursions and settlement expansion can constitute a sustainable political objective. He identifies a potential transition beyond the Netanyahu era as an opportunity to reconsider the relationship between Israeli and Palestinian societies. His central argument is that the continuation of war without a political endgame risks a state of perpetual conflict.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump rejects Iran’s seven-day plan to reopen Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e1be49ecc8ff2bb304bc2ec4f4c6fee58d1900072a23fc4b6c962724b648299</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T02:06:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260926-trump-reportedly-rejects-iran-s-7-day-plan-to-reopen-strait-of-hormuz--f4edda057a7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260926-trump-reportedly-rejects-iran-s-7-day-plan-to-reopen-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Saturday rejected an Iranian plan to reopen the Strait of Hormuz. Iran's Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi presented the proposal to Trump’s envoy Steve Witkoff a day earlier on the sidelines of a UN gathering in New York. The plan stipulated that the important waterway would reopen seven days after an agreement was reached.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
